hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"2961","Narrated to us Al-Rabee' ibn Sulaymaan, narrated to us Ibn Wahb, who informed me Ibn Lahee'ah and Maalik ibn Anas, on the authority of Ibn al-Haad, from Abu Murrah, the freed slave of 'Aqeel ibn Abi Taalib, who said:\n\I entered with 'Abdullah ibn 'Amr ibn al-'Aas upon his father during the days of al-Tashreeq. I saw him eating"","" so he called us to eat. 'Abdullah ibn 'Amr said to him"","" 'I am fasting.' So 'Amr said to him"","" 'Did you not know that these are the days which the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) forbade from fasting and commanded to break the fast?' So he commanded them"","" and they broke their fast. One of them increased over the other.\""\n\nCHAPTER:"""""
